          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"The rose\",\"addressee\":\"The little prince\",\"anchor_quote\":\"je t'aime\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The rose directly avows as true her loving emotional state toward the little prince. Her follow-up says that he had not known this because of her own fault, presenting the avowal as a disclosure and correction of his prior understanding.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"je t'aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Mais oui, je t'aime, lui dit la fleur. Tu n'en a rien su, par ma faute.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.95,\"reason\":\"The focal expression avows love but does not itself undertake a future action, obligation, or continuing relationship. In the surrounding farewell, the rose releases him rather than attaching a promise or demand to the avowal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"je t'aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Tâche d'être heureux...Laisse ce globe tranquille. Je n'en veux plus.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"The expression is represented as a calm, intelligible disclosure rather than a reflex-like affective discharge. Although the separation is emotional, the avowal is embedded in an explanation of what the little prince failed to know.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Il ne comprenait pas cette douceur calme.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Mais oui, je t'aime, lui dit la fleur. Tu n'en a rien su, par ma faute.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"Its core force is adequately captured as a truth-presenting avowal of love. The contextual functions of disclosure, correction, and reassurance do not constitute a distinct core mode beyond T.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"je t'aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Tu n'en a rien su, par ma faute.\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"During the little prince's departure, after apologizing and urging him to be happy, the rose calmly tells him that she loves him and explains that her own conduct prevented him from knowing it. The avowal occurs within a farewell rather than a negotiation of future obligations.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"No undertaking is made by the focal expression. The rose avows love while accepting the little prince's departure and telling him to be happy. The supplied scene shows his surprise and confusion but no explicit verbal uptake of the avowal.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied passages are recognizable as Chapters VIII–IX of Antoine de Saint-Exupéry's Le Petit Prince.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence strongly establishes the represented avowal and supplies corroborating signs of tenderness and grief. It does not provide explicit verbal uptake from the little prince after the focal expression, nor does it establish any specific ongoing commitment created by it.\"}"
        }
      ],
